 "result": "`abort` is defined in `src/tessel/helpers.py:281` and re-exported as `tessel.abort` from `src/tessel/__init__.py:13`.\n\n**How it works:**\n- If an app context is active, it calls `ctx.app.aborter(code, *args, **kwargs)`.\n- Otherwise, it falls back to Werkzeug's `abort` (imported as `_wz_abort`).\n- Either way it raises an `HTTPException` for the status code, and its return type is `NoReturn`.\n\n**Where the aborter comes from:**\n- `aborter_class = Aborter` is declared on the app class in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:165`.\n- `self.aborter = self.make_aborter()` creates the instance (L325), and `make_aborter()` (L496) returns `self.aborter_class()`.\n- An app can override `aborter_class` or `make_aborter` to register custom status codes.",
